# Cross-service staging env contract.
#
# This file is the entry point for the Quinn-owned `infra/cloud/.env.local`
# (NEVER COMMITTED). Copy this file to `infra/cloud/.env.local`, then fill in
# each service's section from the per-service `.env.example` siblings below
# (each per-service file documents the keys with owner + rotation + format).
#
# The bootstrap script (`infra/cloud/scripts/bootstrap-staging.sh`) reads
# `.env.local` and applies each service's TASKS_API_*, BUDGET_API_*, and
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_* prefixed env vars to the corresponding Fly app via
# `fly secrets set`. The prefix is stripped at apply time (e.g.
# TASKS_API_DATABASE_URL -> DATABASE_URL on the Fly app).
#
# ============================================================================
# Service-by-service references
# ============================================================================
#
# tasks-api:
#   infra/cloud/env/tasks-api.env.example
#   Apply prefix: TASKS_API_*
#   Fly app:      sindustries-tasks-api-staging
#
# budget-api:
#   infra/cloud/env/budget-api.env.example
#   Apply prefix: BUDGET_API_*
#   Fly app:      sindustries-budget-api-staging
#
# auto-post-worker (non-HTTP, BullMQ consumer):
#   infra/cloud/env/auto-post-worker.env.example
#   Apply prefix: AUTO_POST_WORKER_*
#   Fly app:      sindustries-auto-post-worker-staging
#
# ============================================================================
# Quinn-owned values (out-of-band; never commit real values to the repo)
# ============================================================================
#
# FLY_API_TOKEN: obtained via `fly auth token` after `fly auth login`.
#   - Used directly by the bootstrap script (CLI invocation).
#   - For CI, register as a GitHub repo secret under the name FLY_API_TOKEN.
#
# Neon staging connection strings: per-schema URLs that the per-service files
# point to with the schema suffix (e.g. ?schema=tasks_api&sslmode=require).
#   - Owner: Quinn.
#   - Rotation: 90d or on-incident.
#
# Upstash staging REDIS_URL: TLS-enabled URL for the BullMQ queue.
#   - Owner: Quinn.
#   - Rotation: per-deploy.
#
# DNS provider token: for sindustries.dev domain / subdomain CNAMEs.
#   - Owner: Quinn.
#   - Workflow files (deploy-staging-*.yml) reference the *name* of this
#     secret only; Quinn registers the value out-of-band.

# ============================================================================
# Template — copy to infra/cloud/.env.local (NEVER COMMIT .env.local)
# ============================================================================
#
# FLY_API_TOKEN=fly_xxx_REPLACE_ME
#
# TASKS_API_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...?schema=tasks_api&sslmode=require
# TASKS_API_REDIS_URL=rediss://default:...@...upstash.io:6379
# TASKS_API_CONTENT_SCHEDULER_REDIS_URL=rediss://default:...@...upstash.io:6379
# TASKS_API_CONTENT_SCHEDULER_API_BASE_URL=https://sindustries-content-scheduler-api-staging.fly.dev/api/v1
# TASKS_API_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://mission-control.sindustries.dev
# TASKS_API_X_CLIENT=real
# TASKS_API_X_HANDLE=sindustries
# TASKS_API_X_API_KEY=...
# TASKS_API_X_API_SECRET=...
# TASKS_API_X_ACCESS_TOKEN=...
# TASKS_API_X_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=...
# TASKS_API_X_ACTOR_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
# TASKS_API_CONTENT_SCHEDULER_INGEST_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
# TASKS_API_CONTENT_SCHEDULER_JOB_ADAPTER=bullmq
# TASKS_API_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector.staging.svc:4318
# TASKS_API_TASKS_API_APPROVAL_USERS=[]
# TASKS_API_TASKS_API_APPROVAL_SERVICE_CREDENTIALS=[]
#
# BUDGET_API_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...?schema=budget_api&sslmode=require
# BUDGET_API_DEV_SESSION_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
# BUDGET_API_BUDGET_API_TOKEN_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
# BUDGET_API_AKAHU_CLIENT_ID=...
# BUDGET_API_AKAHU_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# BUDGET_API_AKAHU_REDIRECT_URI=https://mission-control.sindustries.dev/api/v1/akahu/callback
# BUDGET_API_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://mission-control.sindustries.dev
# BUDGET_API_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector.staging.svc:4318
#
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...?schema=content_scheduler&sslmode=require
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_REDIS_URL=rediss://default:...@...upstash.io:6379
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_CONTENT_SCHEDULER_REDIS_URL=rediss://default:...@...upstash.io:6379
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_CONTENT_SCHEDULER_API_BASE_URL=https://sindustries-content-scheduler-api-staging.fly.dev/api/v1
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_X_CLIENT=real
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_X_HANDLE=sindustries
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_X_API_KEY=...
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_X_API_SECRET=...
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_X_ACCESS_TOKEN=...
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_X_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=...
# AUTO_POST_WORKER_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector.staging.svc:4318
#
# ============================================================================
# Optional Fly app-name overrides (defaults match the fly.toml files)
# ============================================================================
#
# FLY_APP_TASKS_API=sindustries-tasks-api-staging
# FLY_APP_BUDGET_API=sindustries-budget-api-staging
# FLY_APP_AUTO_POST_WORKER=sindustries-auto-post-worker-staging
#
# ============================================================================
# Per-service references
# ============================================================================
# Each per-service file lists every env var Quinn should set, with the prefix
# applied, owner / rotation / format hints, and source-of-truth pointers to
# services/<svc>/.env.example. The bootstrap script does NOT validate that
# .env.local contains every key from the per-service files — it's Quinn's
# responsibility to mirror them. Missing keys will surface as boot-time
# validation failures in the deployed service, not as bootstrap-time errors.